  <div class="status"><i></i>Seeking PhD &amp; research positions</div>
  <p>HAN ZHANG, a CS undergrad in the Turing Class (honors) at <b>Zhejiang University</b>, now a visiting intern at <b>HKUST</b> with Prof. Yuan Liu. I work on <b>3D/4D vision and embodied AI</b>: structured, generalizable representations of geometry, motion and articulation, and how agents learn about a physical world that changes when they touch it.</p>
  <p>The Fool is card zero: a traveler at the cliff's edge, bag over one shoulder, about to step off. That's roughly where I am. I'm <span data-voice="VOLITION|You've read the papers. You've run the ablations. Step off the cliff, kid." tabindex="0">applying for PhDs</span> and open to wherever the road goes next.</p>
  <p>Off the clock I play <span data-voice="ELECTROCHEMISTRY|One more blues lick. Then bed. (It is never one more blues lick.)" tabindex="0">electric guitar</span>, play tennis, and lose whole weekends to <span data-voice="ENCYCLOPEDIA|Fincher, Tarantino, The Godfather. Balatro, Baldur's Gate 3, GTA. This is not procrastination. It is research." tabindex="0">good films and games</span>.</p>
